# Project-Tool Fallbacks
#
# These are TIER 3 tools: a wrong version silently changes output for a given
# repo, so a project that cares must pin its own copy and direnv puts it first
# on PATH. They are declared here anyway, deliberately, as the fallback for
# projects that have not set that up yet.
#
# Declaring them is the honest move: they get installed regardless (by you, by
# an editor, by an agent), so the choice is a declared fallback or silent drift.
# Undeclared is how isort lingered for a year and then broke `brew upgrade`.
#
# CAUTION on formatters: do NOT wire format-on-save to a global fallback. A
# global black against a repo pinned to an older one reformats the whole file
# and hands you a diff you never asked for. Prefer the editor formatting only
# when a project-local formatter resolves.
#
# See docs/PACKAGE_POLICY.md.
brew "black"     # fallback only — projects pin their own
brew "yapf"      # fallback only — projects pin their own
brew "pyright"   # fallback only — eglot resolves project-local first (init-prog-modes.el)

